<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Third Taifa of Niebla</h1><p class="st-meta">1234 CE – 1262 CE (approx.) · capital Niebla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last independent Muslim state of western al-Andalus, ruled by Ibn Mahfuz from Niebla until Alfonso X took it in 1262.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1234, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hud">Ibn Hud's</a> power faded, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mahfuz">Shuayb ibn Muhammad ibn Mahfuz</a> established himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a> and the surrounding district as an independent ruler. After Ferdinand III took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> in 1248, he accepted Castilian overlordship and paid tribute.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The small realm covered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huelva">Huelva</a> and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> region, protected by Niebla's massive walls. As a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mahfuz">Ibn Mahfuz</a> kept internal autonomy, but his isolation between Castilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a> left him little room to manoeuvre.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1262 Alfonso X besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a> for several months, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mahfuz">Ibn Mahfuz</a> surrendered in exchange for lands and income in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. The territory became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1234 CE – 1262 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.26%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1234 CE – 1262 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Niebla</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shuayb ibn Mahfuz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Niebla of Ibn Mahfuz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1248&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-niebla" aria-label="Third Taifa of Niebla on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4513 833 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Third Taifa of Niebla lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4833 1089L4794 1282M4833 1089L4885 950"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 1282h0M4885 950h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4833 1089h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4833 1089h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Niebla. <a href="/atlas?year=1248&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-niebla">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
